What You'll do:

• Administer Microsoft SQL Server databases in production, integrated with Azure cloud services, with strong operational ownership;

• Manage Always-On Availability Groups, Failover Cluster Instances and storage account operations;

• Lead technical resolution of SQL Server incidents: diagnose, remediate and produce structured root cause analysis independently;

• Execute and validate production releases using Azure DevOps and UrbanCode Deploy (UCD);

• Perform query tuning, T-SQL optimization and execution plan analysis;

• Administer and optimize Azure SQL, Azure Pipelines, Azure Monitor and Azure Event Hub;

• Enforce security, permissions management and audit-quality documentation;

• Collaborate with application teams, infrastructure partners and release management;

• Contribute to runbook quality and continuous improvement of database operations.

Who You Are:

• University degree in Computer Science, Engineering or comparable technical field;

• 5-10 years of hands-on experience with Microsoft SQL Server in production environments;

• Proven track record in incident management, production support and performance tuning;

• Strong Azure platform experience is mandatory.

What you'll get:

• Wage according to candidate's professional experience;

- Remote Work whenever possible;

